  "title": "More models, more kinds of input",
  "summary": "November broadened what people can make with Pollinations while making model discovery, Pollen accounting, and API responses more predictable.\n\nPerplexity Sonar, Kimi K2 Thinking, Gemini 3 Pro Preview, Claude Opus 4.5, and other text models joined the lineup. Chat gained reasoning controls and OpenAI-compatible audio input and output; model listings gained capabilities, pricing, and aliases.\n\nRequested dimensions now reach image models more faithfully, Flux reports failures instead of silently switching models, and Nano Banana Pro gained 1K, 2K, and 4K output selection. Enter took on exact-match image caching, with an endpoint to delete cached entries.\n\nEnter added separate tier and pack balances, connected $5–$50 Pollen packs to checkout, and made subscription states easier to read. Spore became the starting tier, while balance caching and tier-lookup fixes reduced avoidable billing round trips and incorrect displays.\n\nOpenAI-compatible paths arrived in Enter, ads left text responses, and streaming, provider-specific fields, upstream errors, image URLs, and request parameters received compatibility fixes. The work makes one API less likely to flatten the differences between the models behind it.",
